    "text": "<p>The variation of equilibrium constant with temperature is given below :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable equalcolumns=\"true\" equalrows=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mi>Temperature</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>EquilibriumConstant</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mtd><mtd><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) respectively, are close to [use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><msup><mi>JK</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]</p>"
